{"name":"Drum Solo","hex":"#a66e4b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"drum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A percussive musical instrument spanned with a thin covering on at least one end for striking, forming an acoustic chamber; a membranophone.","Any similar hollow, cylindrical object."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To beat a drum.","To beat with a rapid succession of strokes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/drum"},{"term":"solo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of music for one performer.","A job or performance done by one person alone."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Without a companion or instructor.","Of, or relating to, a musical solo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Drum solo","blocks":[{"text":"A drum solo is an instrumental solo played on a drum kit. A drum solo may be set or improvised, and of any length, up to being the main performance.\nIn rock, drum solos are unique in that traditionally they are minimally or never accompanied, whereas other instruments may play solos accompanied or unaccompanied. They are also typically free-form in that they do not necessarily adhere to the tempo, style or structure of the song they accompany."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/George_Harrison_and_Ringo_Starr%2C_King%27s_Hall%2C_Belfast_1964_%2818226096790%29_cut_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-George_Harrison_and_Ringo_Starr%2C_King%27s_Hall%2C_Belfast_1964_%2818226096790%29_cut_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drum_solo"},{"title":"Drum","blocks":[{"text":"The drum is a member of the percussion group of musical instruments. In the Hornbostel–Sachs classification system, it is a membranophone. Drums consist of at least one membrane, called a drumhead or drum skin, that is stretched over a shell and struck, either directly with the player's hands, or with a percussion mallet, to produce sound. There is usually a resonant head on the underside of the drum. Other techniques have been used to cause drums to make sound, such as the thumb roll. Drums are the world's oldest and most ubiquitous musical instruments, and the basic design has remained virtually unchanged for thousands of years."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/DrumMozartRegiment.jpg/330px-DrumMozartRegiment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drum"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/TalkingDrum.jpg/500px-TalkingDrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/TalkingDrum.jpg/500px-TalkingDrum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Talking drum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATalkingDrum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Platin_Drums_PTCL2016_AF.jpg/330px-Platin_Drums_PTCL2016_AF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Platin_Drums_PTCL2016_AF.jpg/330px-Platin_Drums_PTCL2016_AF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A drum kit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlatin_Drums_PTCL2016_AF.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Ceremonial_drum.jpg/500px-Ceremonial_drum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Ceremonial_drum.jpg/1280px-Ceremonial_drum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Ceremonial_d